, "start_month": null, "end_year": null, "end_month": null, "expected_count": 1, "cohort": false, "retrieval_hint": {"channel_preference": "fts_keyword", "must_match_phrases": ["Weekly Consolidated Foreign Currency Report", "Major Market Participants", "Net options Euro"], "avoid_phrases": []}}], "computation_spec": {"python_template": "result = abs(values['v2'][0] - values['v1'][0])"}, "output_format": {"type": "number", "unit": "millions", "rounding": 2, "as_percent": false}, "resolution_notes": "The WHO declared COVID-19 a pandemic on March 11, 2020. The question asks for the absolute difference in cumulative net options Euro positions over the 5 weeks preceding and the 5 weeks following the week during which the pandemic was declared, excluding the week of declaration itself. The exact row label for net options Euro positions is uncertain; the provided row hints are guesses based on typical Treasury Bulletin terminology for foreign currency reports. The column hints 'Cumulative 5 weeks preceding' and 'Cumulative 5 weeks following' are also guesses; the actual column labels may differ (e.g., '5 weeks preceding', '5 weeks following', 'Cumulative 5 weeks'). The retrieval hint uses fts_keyword to search for the specific report title and row concept. The years are set to 2020, the year of the pandemic declaration.", "question_kind": "value", "vintage": "latest", "period": null}, "error": null, "elapsed_s": 20.73}
