 for international capital movements likely present monthly net movement figures. We need to sum 12 monthly rows for each category (short term banking funds and brokerage balances) to get the calendar-year total net movement, then compute the difference (brokerage balances minus short term banking funds). The row labels are inferred from typical 1930s Treasury Bulletin tables on international capital movements; exact phrasing may vary. The difference is expressed in billions of dollars, rounded to nearest thousandths place.", "question_kind": "value", "vintage": "latest", "period": "CY"}, "error": null, "elapsed_s": 34.82}
